Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: verba
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: audit what a command says against what it does
 verba runs a command under ptrace and audits what it says against what it
 does: it watches stdout/stderr and the exit code on one side and the real
 file syscalls on the other, then reports every contradiction between the two.
 .
 It is pure C with no runtime dependencies, traces via ptrace (not LD_PRELOAD)
 so static and setuid binaries are in scope, and targets x86-64.
